  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Coastal Pacific Food Distributors has $213M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Coastal Pacific Food Distributors won 9,093 awards this year with an average award size of $23.4K, and obligations are up 49.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations ranged from $110M in FY21 to $213M in FY26, with intermediate totals of $156M in FY22, $140M in FY23, $119M in FY24, and $142M in FY25. All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing is the largest market for Coastal Pacific Food Distributors with $186M in obligations, followed by Commercial Bakeries with $27M. Marine Cargo Handling also appears among the top markets with $58.6K in obligations. The counts and dollar totals above are contract obligations for the fiscal year to date; award-value totals in award tables use total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who is buying from Coastal Pacific Food Distributors?",
        "body": "Federal agencies purchase from Coastal Pacific Food Distributors across multiple food-related markets. All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing accounts for the largest share with $186M in obligations, and Commercial Bakeries accounts for $27M. Marine Cargo Handling accounts for $58.6K in obligations, indicating a smaller niche use case. The company recorded 9,093 awards in FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have Coastal Pacific Food Distributors obligations changed over time?",
        "body": "Obligations for Coastal Pacific Food Distributors rose to $213M in FY26 from $142M in FY25. Prior-year obligations were $119M in FY24, $140M in FY23, $156M in FY22, and $110M in FY21. Year-over-year obligations are up 49.8% for the current fiscal-year-to-date period."
      }
    ]
  },
